      "user_message": "You are an expert Python programmer. Solve the following programming problem.\n\n**Problem: Find Words that Don't Contain a Character**\n\nYou are given a 0-indexed array of strings words and a character x.\nReturn an array of indices representing the words that do not contain the character x.\nNote that the returned array may be in any order.\n\n**Example 1:**\n\nInput: words = [\"leet\",\"code\"], x = \"e\"\nOutput: []\nExplanation: \"e\" occurs in both words: \"leet\", and \"code\". Hence, we return an empty array.\n\n**Example 2:**\n\nInput: words = [\"abc\",\"bcd\",\"aaaa\",\"cbc\"], x = \"a\"\nOutput: [1]\nExplanation: \"a\" occurs in \"abc\", and \"aaaa\". Hence, we return index 1 because it's the word that doesn't contain 'a'.\n\n**Example 3:**\n\nInput: words = [\"abc\",\"bcd\",\"aaaa\",\"cbc\"], x = \"z\"\nOutput: [0,1,2,3]\nExplanation: \"z\" does not occur in any of the words. Hence, we return indices of all words.\n\n**Constraints:**\n\n1 <= words.length <= 50\n1 <= words[i].length <= 50\nx is a lowercase English letter.\nwords[i] consists only of lowercase English letters.\n\nUse the following starter code and return the complete implementation:\n\n```python\nclass Solution:\n    def findWordsContaining(self, words: List[str], x: str) -> List[int]:\n```\n\nReturn only the final Python solution inside one fenced code block.",
